---
import DocPage from "../../layouts/DocPage.astro";

const title = "sf-intelligence vs Salesforce DX MCP - sf-intelligence";
const description =
  "Compare sf-intelligence with Salesforce DX MCP Server: read-only org intelligence for impact, permissions, and docs vs DevOps retrieve and deploy workflows.";

const jsonld = [
  {
    "@type": "FAQPage",
    mainEntity: [
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        name: "Can sf-intelligence replace the Salesforce DX MCP Server?",
        acceptedAnswer: {
          "@type": "Answer",
          text: "No - they solve different problems. The DX MCP Server is for DevOps: deploy, retrieve, run Apex, LWC scaffolding. sf-intelligence is for read-only org understanding: impact analysis, permissions tracing, dependency graphs, and documentation. Many teams use both.",
        },
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        name: "Is sf-intelligence safer for production orgs?",
        acceptedAnswer: {
          "@type": "Answer",
          text: "sf-intelligence has no write path - it cannot deploy, edit, or delete anything in Salesforce. The DX MCP Server includes write-capable DevOps tools. For exploring a production org's metadata safely, sf-intelligence's read-only guarantee is the differentiator.",
        },
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        name: "Does sf-intelligence work offline?",
        acceptedAnswer: {
          "@type": "Answer",
          text: "Yes. After one read-only retrieve, answers come from a local vault with no network calls. The DX MCP Server calls Salesforce APIs during tool use.",
        },
      },
    ],
  },
];
---

<DocPage
  title={title}
  description={description}
  path="/compare/salesforce-dx-mcp"
  heading="sf-intelligence vs Salesforce DX MCP Server"
  intro="Both are Salesforce MCP servers. They are <strong>complementary, not competing</strong> - one is for DevOps, the other for read-only org intelligence. This page helps you pick the right tool (or both)."
  crumbs={[{ label: "compare", href: "/compare/salesforce-dx-mcp" }]}
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: "sf-intelligence vs Salesforce DX MCP", path: "/compare/salesforce-dx-mcp" }]}
  jsonld={jsonld}
>
  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <div class="prose">

        <h2 id="summary">At a glance</h2>
        <table class="doc-table">
          <thead><tr><th></th><th>sf-intelligence</th><th>Salesforce DX MCP Server</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><strong>Maintainer</strong></td><td>Community (MIT + Commons Clause)</td><td>Salesforce (official)</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Primary purpose</strong></td><td>Understand an org - impact, permissions, docs</td><td>DevOps - deploy, retrieve, run code</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Write to org</strong></td><td><strong>No</strong> - read-only retrieve only</td><td>Yes - deploy, edit, run Apex/tests</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Default mode</strong></td><td>Offline (local vault)</td><td>Live API per tool call</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Dependency graph</strong></td><td>Yes - DuckDB, confidence-tagged edges</td><td>No dedicated graph</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Impact / blast radius</strong></td><td>Core feature</td><td>Not a focus</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Permission tracing</strong></td><td>Yes - FLS, sharing cascade</td><td>Limited</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Plain-language routing</strong></td><td>Semantic router, host LLM picks the tools</td><td>Tool-per-task model</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Cost</strong></td><td>Free</td><td>Free (official)</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>npm package</strong></td><td><code>sf-intelligence</code></td><td><code>@salesforce/mcp</code> (via Salesforce CLI)</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>

        <h2 id="when-sfi">Choose sf-intelligence when you need to…</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Ask "what breaks if I delete this field?" before making a change</li>
          <li>Trace why a user cannot see a record or edit a field</li>
          <li>Document an inherited org (data dictionary, architecture overview)</li>
          <li>Explore a production org with zero write risk</li>
          <li>Work offline after a single retrieve (airplane, VPN-restricted environments)</li>
          <li>Get provenance and confidence labels on every answer</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="when-dx">Choose the DX MCP Server when you need to…</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Deploy or retrieve metadata from an AI-assisted workflow</li>
          <li>Run Apex, execute tests, scaffold LWC</li>
          <li>Use first-party Salesforce DevOps tooling in MCP</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="both">Use both together</h2>
        <p>A common pattern: use sf-intelligence to <strong>understand</strong> the blast radius and permissions landscape, then use the DX MCP Server to <strong>implement</strong> the change. Register both MCP servers in the same Claude Code or Cursor project - they do not conflict.</p>

        <h2 id="more">More comparisons</h2>
        <p>See how sf-intelligence compares with the paid cloud platforms: <a href="/compare/elements-cloud">vs Elements.cloud</a> and <a href="/compare/sweep">vs Sweep</a>.</p>

        <div class="callout"><p><strong>Disclaimer:</strong> This comparison is based on publicly documented capabilities as of 2026. Salesforce's official MCP offerings evolve - verify current feature sets in Salesforce's official documentation. sf-intelligence is not affiliated with Salesforce.</p></div>

        <div style="padding-top:36px;">
          <div class="cta-box">
            <h2 class="screen-type">Try the read-only side.</h2>
            <p>Free on npm. Install alongside your existing MCP servers.</p>
            <div class="cta-actions">
              <a class="btn btn-solid" href="/getting-started">install sf-intelligence</a>
              <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/mcp">MCP overview</a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</DocPage>
